# AGENTS.md — branch `ai4r_ccv2`

## Branch purpose (read first)
This branch is a deliberate scope reset. It is base JiuwenSwarm plus the preserved Codex integration plus a new Capability Capsule (CC) v2 runner exposed to agents as native tools.

The M1 research machinery was removed on purpose: the Intention/intent Compiler, the old capsule pipeline and `capsule_runtime`, `jiuwenswarm/research*`, the RSI console, ccbench/harbor benchmarks and `deploy/m1`. **Do not restore, extend or re-create them, and do not follow the M1 PRD / TASKS / Spec Kit process that earlier versions of this file described.** The old file is kept on `AI4Research-Main` and in git history.

Start here instead:
- `docs/architecture/README.md` — what the branch is and how the pieces fit
- `docs/architecture/ccv2/README.md` — install, start, demo
- `docs/architecture/ccv2/PROVENANCE.md` — base and source revisions
- `docs/architecture/ccv2/PROTOCOL-CHANGES.md` — changes made to the CC protocol, with evidence
- `jiuwenswarm/ccv2/` — the runner; `demo/ccs/` — demonstration CCs

## Working rules
1. Build real things; no reports, audits or tests that were not asked for. Fix the pipeline in general; never hard-code a result to make a check pass.
2. Do not label a simulation as a live-agent or image result. Tests are distinct from live runs.
3. Keep the protocol lightweight: no registry service, planner or intent compiler.
4. Preserve unrelated work and credentials; never write secrets into artifacts. Do not commit, push, merge or deploy unless asked.
5. 5175 is the only local web host port.
6. Codex integration lives in `jiuwenswarm/server/runtime/codex_subscription/`, `agent_adapter/interface_codex.py`, `gateway_adapter/codex_adapter.py` and `jiuwenswarm/codex_start.py`. Keep them free of imports from removed packages.

## Factory feature (amended)
The iterative inference factory has a feature-scoped exception for its evidence-driven controller; follow [AMENDMENT.md](docs/architecture/factory/AMENDMENT.md). The host enforces authority and lifecycle; the agent chooses actions. Do not restore M1. See [MIGRATION.md](docs/architecture/factory/MIGRATION.md) for old-to-new behavior, planned components, legacy-config errors and rollback. All existing rules remain in force outside that amendment.
# Architecture: JiuwenSwarm + Capability Capsules v2 (`ai4r_ccv2`)

## What this branch is for
A reduced JiuwenSwarm in which a real agent discovers, reads and uses Capability Capsules (CCs) through a small runner. Base JiuwenSwarm and the Codex-as-model integration are kept. The earlier AI4Research M1 machinery (intent compiler, old capsule pipeline, RSI console, benchmarks, its design package) was removed on purpose and is not documented here. It remains in git history and on `AI4Research-Main`.

## How the pieces fit
```
Codex (model, ChatGPT login)        jiuwenswarm/server/runtime/codex_subscription/
        |  agent mode (opt-in: JIUWENSWARM_CODEX_AGENT=1; workspace-write sandbox, shell + patch)
        v
JiuwenSwarm agent  --MCP stdio-->   jiuwenswarm/ccv2/agent_mcp.py   (8 tools: cc_list, cc_describe,
                                    cc_material, cc_artifact, cc_call, cc_start, cc_instance, cc_stop)
                                         |
                                         v
                                    jiuwenswarm/ccv2/ccv2.py   Host: prepare, call, start, stop, receipts
                                         |                      applications.py: image services (docker CLI)
                          +--------------+--------------+
                          v                             v
                 native binding                  image binding
                 process, JSON on stdin/out      docker run, pinned local image id, --pull=never
```
- **Authority** comes only from operator flags (`--grant`, `--workspace`, `--allow-built`). The model cannot widen it.
- **Native CCs** are cheap local clients and inspectors and are not sandboxed. **Image CCs** carry an application with its own OS and runtime and are started, probed and stopped by the host.
- **Passive materials** (methodology, ontology) are readable and grant nothing. A **request CC** states a desired service and is not callable; the agent builds the implementation, which becomes an ordinary CC.

