18-## Build order
19-
20:1. **Static template first.** A person writes the template for the fixed path Search, Screening, Hypothesis, Builder, Research Benchmark, Scientific Evaluation, Delivery. It runs after the Intention Compiler node. This follows PRD section 2: the static default comes before dynamic planning.
21-2. **Planner second.** The Planner CC produces a `plan_proposal` that uses the same node shape. The same binder checks it and the same freeze produces a `run_plan`. The scheduler, check runner and dispatch records are the same for both. Only `plan_source` differs (`static` or `planned`).
22-3. **The plan source is chosen before the run starts.** The run request carries `plan_source` (`static` or `planned`, default `static`) and nothing else selects it ([D39](../method/decisions.md#d39), [run request](field-catalog.md#client-submission)). A failed Planner does not switch to the template. A rejected or infeasible plan, from either plan source, records `plan_infeasible` and halts the run. See [plan outcome](#plan-outcome).
