414-### Freeze
415-
416:After freeze the scheduler may not replan, substitute a CC, change a pin or edit a limit. Later library, bundle or policy changes do not affect the run. A changed graph or objective needs a new plan, a new binding and a new freeze, as a new run. Future input values stay references. At dispatch the scheduler binds each `future_output` input only to an output that the producer node's gate accepted. A rejected output is never bound. It builds each `host_record` input from the accepted records of the run: the receipt of the accepted Builder attempt for `build_receipt`, one entry per accepted node attempt that is an ancestor of the Delivery node, naming its node-scope gate decision, for `gate_decision_index`, the accepted Screening result for `screening_result`, the accepted Benchmark receipts for `execution_receipt` and `provisioning_receipt`, and the run's prepared lock and frozen configuration for `environment_lock` and `run_configuration`.
417-
418-## From run plan node to execution contracts
419-
420:At dispatch the scheduler builds the contracts of one attempt from one frozen node. It chooses nothing. It copies or derives every value, so the contracts cannot widen what the plan pinned. The contracts are the [Node Execution Contract](node-execution.md#enclosing-node) (node scope) and its [Subnode Execution Contracts](node-execution.md#concrete-subnode).
421-
422-Two identities tie every record of an attempt together.
